grand theft auto 5 is consistently one  of the best-selling games each week  almost 10 years after it was originally  released yeah bet that makes you feel  old because it certainly does me i  remember watching the announcement  trailer for gta 5 back when i was in  college uh excuse me while i have a  michael like midlife crisis here i'm i'm  i'm gonna need some hot coffee however  like me gta 5 may be showing its age  because we're finally starting to get  our first hints of grand theft auto 6.  with rockstar recently confirming that  development of the game is quote well  underway and rumors constantly swirling  about new characters and the game's  location yet while gta 5 and gta online  remain popular to this day it's clear  after the tragic launch of grand theft  auto the trilogy definitive edition that  even the mightiest of video game  franchises can't rest on its laurels so  i put together my list of what i want  for the franchise that skipped an entire  generation of consoles to do in order to  update itself for today  number one a new setting but not in the  present day okay i'm going to start off  my list a little bit controversially  because some people just want to see the  comments section burn while it has not  been confirmed a lot of rumors and  unconfirmed leaks have pointed to gta 6  set to take a return to the seminole by  city the franchise has passed each  version of miami florida and many fans  have actually been excited to possibly  find themselves back in the world of the  80s style gangsters pastel suits and  palm trees however some fans such as  myself have never really been beach  people and even more so think it's time  for the series to branch out from  constantly returning to old haunts and  try something new what would a chicago  new orleans or austin feel like in the  twisted world of grand theft auto or  even further how about stepping outside  of the united states and give us a look  at somewhere like london and yes i know  the series has actually gone there  before but it would be cool to actually  see gta's version of london in three  dimensions this time however one thing  the series should steal from vice city  is a non-present day setting vice city's  80s vibe is what helped make that entry  stand out so perhaps a game set in the  70s or 90s could also lend this new  installment a much needed sense of style  and identity plus if it's set during the  90s we could maybe bring pogs back into  style and who doesn't want pogs to  return  number two multiple protagonists yeah i  know i must hate myself because i'm  doubling down on the controversial  choices here one of the most polarizing  aspects of gta 5 was its choice to  feature multiple protagonists in its  main story and certainly this decision  came with mixed results in terms of the  actual plot however for me i think it  actually lent a truly unique ability for  the game to make the world feel more  alive i adored jumping between different  characters to just see what each of them  was doing when i returned to them like  michael doing yoga in his fancy house or  franklin walking the streets of downtown  or  whatever the hell trevor was up to me  the psycho no  you are the craziest chick i've ever met  i love you you're thin you're  irrationally angry nothing you say makes  any sense you are  completely have no control of your  emotions we have nothing in common oh  baby we're made for each other prove it  it instantly put you into the feel of  each character to get to see their  varied ways of existing within the city  with a tighter narrative this varied  perspective could help give the game's  story some much needed lengths and yet  continue to evolve the risks taken in  gta 5 without back pedaling on them hell  you could even marry this idea with the  concept of different time zones from my  last entry with each character possibly  living in a different time period of the  same city allowing for the series to  truly take a big risk with the formula  and show off the rockstar team's  creative skill  number three a female protagonist this  one should hopefully not be a shock to  anybody despite being one of the oldest  and biggest gaming franchises that's  still thriving grand theft auto has  never centered a female playable  character in any of its mainline games  in fact  it's kind of an understatement to say  that grand theft auto hasn't really been  known to treat women uh  well let's just say what kind of [ __ ]  animal do you take me for no i didn't  kill him  but i did kidnap his wife oh no  oh [ __ ] and while that may have been  overlooked in previous entries it would  be deeply disappointing for a new  iteration to continue that trend but  even more so i don't want the game to  just add a female protagonist just for  the sake of it just to you know mark off  that checkbox but i actually think it  would inject a much needed storytelling  vibrancy to see a woman within the  criminal world of the grand theft auto  games most women in gangster types of  storylines get relegated to the role of  wife or girlfriend so it would actually  allow the series to add a fresh twist to  a somewhat stale genre what would it be  like for a woman to rise to prominence  in the mob world or hell why not feature  a woman who gets to be as over-the-top  bonkers as trevor was in gta 5. having a  woman yank herself into the driver's  seat of the franchise could be a cool  way to see this world with fresh eyes  number four a stronger narrative while  the characters of grand theft auto games  have consistently been their strength  its plot sadly has not been while it was  interesting to see trevor's antics or  michael's midlife crisis in grand theft  auto 5 the actual story descended into a  convoluted mess of conspiracies and  heists the same thing happened in grand  theft auto 4 with nico being a fairly  intriguing lead left to languish in a  pretty standard tale  life is complicated i  i never thought i'd live like this  no  when the war came i did bad things and  after the war i thought nothing of doing  bad things in fact to my mind san  andreas is the only game in the series  to ever nail telling a truly engaging  narrative front to back yet it's clear  that rockstar can tell a strong  narrative with the red dead redemption  games being some of the most unique and  memorable stories of the past few  generations of gaming so why not bring  that same level of craft to the grand  theft auto series and truly tell a story  worthy of the game's legacy  but with that said that brings me to  number five more grounded insanity look  we all know that the grand theft auto  games can get pretty bonkers especially  when you play around in the game's  sandbox i mean personally my favorite  thing to do playing grand theft auto  growing up was to use cheat codes to  become invincible spawn a rocket  launcher and then just start shooting  everything that moved until an army of  tanks showed up and that same level of  off the wall antics has continued into  grand theft auto online yet in the year  since grand theft auto 5's release the  saints row series has come and gone and  possibly may even come back again and  over the course of that franchise it  went from lighthearted parody of the  grand theft auto games to straight-up  alien invasion superhero antics it kind  of feels like the era of parody in these  types of games reached its zenith a few  years ago so for grand theft auto 6  while i would still want to have those  over the top moments here and there  lending the story a more grounded  sensibility overall may be the way to go  so that when those bigger moments do  happen they feel like true climaxes  instead of tired parody  number six a more lived in world open  world games have really evolved in the  years since grand theft auto 5 released  and while the more aimless feel may have  been acceptable in 2013 it's certainly  showing its age in 2022 games like red  dead or the witcher or the recently  released elden ring have shown that it's  possible to have a large sprawling world  that also still feels like they exist  beyond just being a playground for your  player character having npcs live their  own lives and there being just generally  more casual things to do around the  world is a must for a new gta in fact we  should also see more interior locations  too ensuring that the gta world doesn't  just feel like one big outdoor area with  some buildings in it to navigate around  but a true living breathing city  number seven improved fighting mechanics  okay so i'm not asking for the grand  theft auto games to become sifu or  anything like that because the series  gameplay focus should always remain on  its guns yet i think we can all kind of  admit that punching in grand theft auto  games has never really felt fun outside  of maybe san andreas one of the best  things grand theft auto 6 could do is  actually make punching out random  pedestrians on the street feel  oh so so satisfying adding in a few  small fighting mechanics could go a long  way to making the gameplay feel fresh  number eight rpg light elements now i  don't want gta to go all assassin's  creed on us and turn away from its  arcade roots into a more grounded rpg  however one fun element of san andreas  was its light rpg elements allowing you  to really craft your character in your  own unique way staying fit or building  up stats was a lot of fun and in return  to some of those elements could be a  cool way to really build upon previous  entries in the franchise plus being  honest i'll probably just end up only  eating fast food like i do in real life  good talk radio it goes without saying  that any grand theft auto game worth  itself should feature an iconic  soundtrack however my personal favorite  thing in any grand theft auto game has  got to be the talk radio channels i have  a ton of fond memories of listening to  the hilariously over the top npr station  while playing liberty city stories on my  psp you've alienated all your friends  huh have you yeah mostly because i  listen to your show all the time and i  tell people they should live by your  advice oh yeah i did own a psp and  actually i still have it also by the way  i dug this out for this little bit in  this video and i didn't check what was  inside it and i found that i had a copy  of spider-man 2 in it like the movie not  the game do you all remember when we  were told that we would be watching  movies on this thing like umd's are the  way of the future uh the past is weird  but coincidentally speaking of  spider-man games like marvel spider-man  and its spin-off miles morales have  continued this talk radio trend with j  jonah jameson's rant and conspiracy fuel  podcast being one of the most fun  world-building elements of those games  people i always thought spider-man was a  few geese sort of a gaggle but this  confirms it as if that atrocious white  spider wasn't enough i've had repeated  sightings of him  in a new outfit some sort of punk rock  inspired thing that makes sane people  want to tear out their eyeballs with a  rusty spoon sadly though the talk radio  shows of grand theft auto 5 were fairly  lackluster so it would behoove any new  entry of the grand theft auto franchise  to help restore the series glory days  and bring us some new talk shows single  player dlc yeah i know i'm probably  getting a little bit ahead of myself  thinking about dlc before the main game  is even out but i think gta 5 fans have  all felt the disappointment at the lack  of single player additional content for  the game rather given the cash cow that  is gta online rockstar has instead  focused mainly on building out its  multiplayer component instead while  there have been some single-player  missions here and there for gta like the  recent franklin story missions they felt  few and far between and more like side  quests than true big additions to the  gta world yet while single player dlc  may not be as money generating as its  online counterparts some of grand theft  auto 4's best moments came from its dlc  additions the ballad of gay tony and the  lost and the damned so in addition to  just a greater focus on single player in  the main game it would be a welcome  return to form for gta 6 to give us even  more bonkers and risk taking side  stories in additional dlc  that's my list for what i want in grand  theft auto 6 but i know a lot of my  choices were probably let's just say  divisive so i'd love to hear your  thoughts below would you rather return  to vice city do you think the franchise  should actually go even more over the  top instead and what else would you like  to see i'd love to hear all that down in  the comments below and don't forget to  like and subscribe to this channel for  more gta coverage as it comes out and if  you can't wait you can check out our  rankings for all the grand theft auto  games but until then i am going to start  replaying vice city stories on my psp  and i thank you so much for watching  [Music]

